pen_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-6558](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-6558)\r\n### Description\n\nThe histogram statistics collected using ANALYZE for range sharded tables seems to be inaccurate. \r\n\r\nI created a table with column id with values between 1 and 100k and ran ANALYZE on the query. I plotted the histogram generated and it looks as follows.\r\n\r\n```\r\nCREATE TABLE t_100k (id INT, PRIMARY KEY (id ASC));\r\nINSERT INTO t_100k SELECT s FROM generate_series(1, 100000) s;\r\nANALYZE t_100k;\r\nSELECT s.stavalues1 FROM \r\n    pg_statistic s JOIN pg_class c ON s.starelid = c.oid JOIN pg_attribute a ON a.attrelid = c.oid AND s.staattnum = a.attnum WHERE a.attname='id' AND c.relname='t_range_pk_100k';\r\n```\r\n\r\n![Histogram](https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/assets/564644/5a8951ef-37b1-414a-805f-cc2e0c804f95)\r\n\r\nIf the primary key is HASH indexed then the histogram seems fairly uniform as expected.\n\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\n\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\n\n[DB-6558]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-6558?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/17367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/17367/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":9261625523,"node_id":"REFE_lADOBlCVUc5l_aJczwAAAAIoCTCz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/9261625523","actor":{"login":"tanujnay112","id":3924842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjQ4NDI=","avatar_u